#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186068657 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186068815 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "623f9081-96b8-53f5-8881-b17bea5d0316" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Volume of a Solid Using the Shell Method"}] :question/id #uuid "29e835eb-531e-5241-911f-45e2d686b183" :question/math-academy-id "e-8853" :question/problem "Consider the finite region bounded by the curve $x=2y-2y^2$ and the $y$-axis, as shown below. Calculate the volume of the solid generated when this region is rotated $2\\pi$ radians about the $x$-axis.\n\n![](images/c3/c34f58201d91a5490379127a64782b05bd7e7bdea7723109cee11587d019cb29.png)" :question/worked-solution "First, we determine the points where the curve intersects the $y$-axis by solving the following equation for $y$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n2y - 2y^{2} &= 0 \\\\\n2y(1 - y) &= 0\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe solutions are $y=0$, and $y=1$. So, we need to integrate from $y=0$ to $y=1$.\n\nUsing the shell method, the volume of the solid can be found as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nV &= 2π\\int_{c}^{d}yf(y)dy \\\\\n&= 2π\\int_{0}^{1}y(2y - 2y^{2})dy \\\\\n&= 4π\\int_{0}^{1}(y^{2} - y^{3})dy \\\\\n&= 4π(\\int_{0}^{1}y^{2}dy - \\int_{0}^{1}y^{3}dy) \\\\\n&= \\left.4π(\\frac{y^{3}}{3}\\right|_{0}^{1} - \\left.\\frac{y^{4}}{4}\\right|_{0}^{1}) \\\\\n&= 4π((\\frac{1}{3} - 0) - (\\frac{1}{4} - 0)) \\\\\n&= 4π(\\frac{1}{3} - \\frac{1}{4}) \\\\\n&= \\frac{π}{3}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186068658 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186068816 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "49361606-6120-5b9c-888f-0cdaf012f125" :knowledge-point/title "Constructing an Integral Representing the Volume of a Solid"}] :question/id #uuid "77659797-1ecc-567e-b864-cfb39c21b0c0" :question/math-academy-id "e-8856" :question/problem "![](images/cf/cf4e624293586613b00a7209cd40a89b5303f0495c2fba36d751660ae7f8a91b.png)\n\nConsider the finite region bounded by the curve $x=4y-y^2$ and the $y$-axis, as shown above. Using the shell method, find an integral that gives the volume of the solid generated when that region is rotated $2\\pi$ radians about the $x$-axis." :question/worked-solution "First, we determine the points where the curve intersects the $y$-axis by solving the following equation for $y$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n4y - y^{2} &= 0 \\\\\ny(4 - y) &= 0\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe solutions are $y=0, \\, 4$. So, we need to integrate from $y=0$ to $y=4$.\n\nUsing the shell method, the volume of the solid can be expressed as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nV &= 2π\\int_{c}^{d}yf(y)dy \\\\\n&= 2π\\int_{0}^{4}y(4y - y^{2})dy\n\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186069023 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186068816 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "49361606-6120-5b9c-888f-0cdaf012f125" :knowledge-point/title "Constructing an Integral Representing the Volume of a Solid"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "81061f46-c5ec-52eb-bef6-55a18e9ef911" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2π\\displaystyle \\int_{0}^{2}y(y - 2y^{2})dy" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186065572} {:answer/id #uuid "c172a667-33c4-5ea5-b951-fedd539b2456" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2π\\displaystyle \\int_{0}^{1/2}y(y - 2y^{2})dy" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186065573} {:answer/id #uuid "fb8c9599-981d-5850-8e21-a397c824ef86" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "π\\displaystyle \\int_{0}^{1/2}(y - 2y^{2})^{2}dy" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186065574} {:answer/id #uuid "01686851-8c14-5a81-8625-871e9b997d6f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2π\\displaystyle \\int_{0}^{1/2}(y - 2y^{2})dy" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186065575} {:answer/id #uuid "24d8acdc-6f0f-5148-8a9d-207c5080b4dd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "π\\displaystyle \\int_{0}^{2}(y - 2y^{2})^{2}dy" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186065576}] :answer-field/id #uuid "4c1fb730-89df-5930-9ffd-4e3c7d99d7df" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186065571}] :question/id #uuid "5e4f431c-c20b-5b36-b61b-0c45e3b37d9b" :question/math-academy-id "q-11403" :question/problem "Consider the finite region bounded by the curve $x = y - 2y^{2}$ and the $y$-axis. What integral gives the volume of the solid generated when that region is rotated $2π$ radians about the $x$-axis?"}]}
